Legend (canonical)

Solid arrows (↓) = control path: intent → plans → actions. 

Dotted arrows (↑) = telemetry path: actions/state → lineage/metrics → human + governance. 

Red constraint arrows = constraint supremacy / injection from Governance into Engine, TG, and contracts. 

Lineage spine (L) = immutable ancestry trace binding all layers. 


Narrative walkthrough (Appendix-L style)

1. Human primacy entry. Human intent is expressed through an Alignment Surface (AS) and normalized into a Structured Intent Object (I). 


2. Constraint + budget consolidation. Governance Kernel and Policy Engine generate Constraint Vector C and pin it into the Engine; budgets B are mandatory inputs to EC. 


3. RB/AB gating. The Engine computes RB per TG node and selects the admissible AB under GK rules. 


4. Planning + contracting. E expands intent into TG, then binds MCP contracts (capabilities, AB ceiling, cost caps) before delegation to agents. 


5. Execution with bounded capability. Agents execute TG nodes under contracts and constraints; they never originate goals or cross RB. 


6. Telemetry + co-evolution. Agent outputs and realized costs flow upward to E; E commits lineage, updates SI/HSS/SCP, and may promote/demote AB.
